      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elevated-temperature degradation of this alloy is governed by selective grain-boundary oxidation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grain boundaries act as fast diffusion pathways that enable localized chemical segregation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cr and Al are oxidation-active elements capable of promoting protective oxide scales.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC13208696::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "In an oxidizing atmosphere, Cr and Al oxidize preferentially at the grain boundaries of the target alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC13208696::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidation causes local Cr and Al depletion at the grain boundaries.",
